From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] host: keep power save off by default

With CONFIG_CFG80211_DEFAULT_PS=y, the default of the kernel, cfg80211
sets WIPHY_FLAG_PS_ON_BY_DEFAULT and calls set_power_mgmt with "on" when
the station interface comes up.  Since the driver has set_power_mgmt,
this turns on the modem sleep of the firmware at each boot: ping through
the access point took 150 ms on average instead of 11 ms.  The firmware
starts with WIFI_PS_NONE for a low RX latency, so clear the flag.
"iw dev wlan0 set power_save on" still turns it on.

Upstream: not sent
---
--- a/host/esp_cfg80211.c
+++ b/host/esp_cfg80211.c
@@ -2872,6 +2872,8 @@
 	/* set caps */
 	wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_AP_PROBE_RESP_OFFLOAD;
 	wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_REPORTS_OBSS;
+	/* The firmware starts with power save off: report it so. */
+	wiphy->flags &= ~WIPHY_FLAG_PS_ON_BY_DEFAULT;
 	//wiphy->features |= NL80211_CMD_PROBE_CLIENT;
 	wiphy->features |= NL80211_FEATURE_SK_TX_STATUS;
 
